Dear Philip /BAHBAO (ric),



Pls forward the technician's full report on his findings on FSCU5693437.



Alarm 306 indicates high pressure switch has activated, discharge pressure has exceeded 22bar.

Aside from defective controller Alarm 306 could be due to variety of causes: refrigerant overcharge, high ambient temperature, defective high pressure switch (or its cable/wiring) or pressure transmitter, defective condenser fan motor (or it's wiring or contactor), etc.



If parts were not available, technician could just have swapped parts from an empty unit, instead of reworking the cargo to another unit - which could have minimized re-handling and risk of re-exposure of the cargo, and the same time save reworking and trucking costs.





Dear Mr. Park / COE (ric),



FSCU5693437 is under warranty. But STARCOOL do not have an agent in BHBAH.

Understand you arerequesting STARCOOL to improve service quality in middle the middle East region. Hope their after sales service network is enhanced soon.



Tks/Brgds,

E. Mesa



