Dear Shaji,



Re: Malfunctioning of Export Reefer Contr No.FSCU5693437

      Cargo: Frozen Cut Crabs

      Set Temp: minius 18 deg C

      To be loaded on HNBW0169E ETA Bah 27.07.13



Reference telecon, Port Authorities advised today morning that the above reefer is malfunctioning. We have arranged reefer technician on urgent basis who have checked the reefer and advised that "Alarm 306 which is high pressure switch ( when compressor starts to work for some minutes condensor fan gets off and as a result of this, pressure goes high and compressor also cuts off. In view of this, controller is suspected to be malfunctioning)Supply/Return at 1100hrs: -9.0C / -7.0C.

As spare parts not available, technician recommended to cross stuff the cargo.



We have taken special approval from the customs and arranged to take out the malfunctioning export reefer container outside port to Shipper's cold store for de-stuffing the cargo. Also have arranged another empty reefer container for PTI and stuffing the cargo which has been de-stuffed to shipper's cold store.



Will advise the Charges incurred once the opertion is completed.



SINWOG: Empty malfunction reefer container FSCU5693437 will be loaded to JEA on HNBW0169E. Please advise final destination



Rgds/Philip

