<div><font size="2" face="Calibri"></font>&nbsp;</div>
<div><font color="#0000ff" size="2" face="Calibri"><u>Further we also need Carrier, Thermoking, Daikin also to hv their official representation in Bahrain.</u></font></div>
<div><u><font color="#0000ff" size="2" face="Calibri">Both vendors hv experienced technicians, and had trainings from Dubai (from official agent of respective makers in Dubai).</font></u></div>
<div><u><font color="#0000ff" size="2" face="Calibri">If the exercise can be done once more and officially declare BAHBA vendors as official agent of respective makers (with ample/sufficient spare parts).</font></u></div>
<div><u><font color="#0000ff" size="2" face="Calibri">Then Bahrain too wud become a full fledged reefer handling terminal, (after AEJEA, AEKLF).</font></u></div>
<div><font size="2" face="Calibri"></font>&nbsp;</div>
<div><font color="#800040" size="2" face="Calibri">Have you taken up with Star cool on the shortage/in-sufficient spare part at AEAUH vendor (MECRC Abu Dhabi), whereby we experienced severe issue and had to incurr huge cost to safeguard the cargo (transporting
 mty from JEA trmnl to AUH trmnl to remove the spare).</font></div>
<div><font color="#800040" size="2" face="Calibri">U/stand all Makers agents keep only regular spare needed (which is exposing risk to liners who use these agents svcs).&nbsp; It should be the Maker who should be supplying to these agents certain parts which are
 expensive but not regularly used at free of cost for stocking purposes.</font></div>
<div><font size="2" face="Calibri"></font>&nbsp;</div>
<div><font size="2" face="Calibri">Bahrain Trmnl is managed by APMT, but without any official Reefer Vendor (except just monitoring) and we outsource reefer vendor as abv for to meet irregularities.</font></div>
<div><font size="2" face="Calibri"></font>&nbsp;</div>
